name: sim.setThreadAutomaticSwitch
description: 
luaSynopsis: int previousLockLevel=sim.setThreadAutomaticSwitch(bool allowAutoSwitch / int lockLevel)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. allowAutoSwitch: if false, then the thread will not be automatically interrupted anymore (i.e. automatic thread switching will be temporarily disabled). Calling n times sim.setThreadAutomaticSwitch(false) requires to call n times sim.setThreadAutomaticSwitch(true) to restore the initial behaviour.
2. lockLevel: allows to set an auto switch lock level: a level > 0 indicates that automatic thread interruption is disabled.
3. Best is to always use following to temporarily lock automatic thread interruptions:
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. previousLockLevel: the lock level before calling the function, i.e. the lock level that should be restored later on.
